# NLSY79: Age and DISSAVED — Analysis Results

Data: data/nls_bmi_processed.csv, n=12,686 respondents, 9 cols, 0 missing.
AGE range 24-32 (9 values). P(DISSAVED=1)=0.2355 full file.

## Key data-quality finding
2,200 rows have INCOME and BMI both set to the file-wide column means (mean
imputation); among them DISSAVED=0 in 2,178/2,200 (99.0%) — savings variables
default-imputed to 0. These rows are older (mean AGE 29.0 vs 27.6). The 2,151
"exact duplicate" rows are collisions among these imputed rows (limited
GENDER x AGE combos), not copies of the same person.
Excluding imputed rows: n=10,486, P(DISSAVED=1)=0.2829, corr(AGE,DISSAVED)=+0.016.

## Models (logistic, AGE centered at 27.86; BMI>100 rows [n=11] dropped)
### FULL file, adjusted (n=12,675): DISSAVED ~ AGE_c + AGE_c2 + GENDER + log1p(INCOME) + BMI + BLACK + HISPANIC
- AGE_c:  -0.049 (SE 0.009, z=-5.23, p<0.001), OR=0.952
- AGE_c2: -0.009 (SE 0.004, z=-2.00, p=0.045), OR=0.991
- LR test quadratic: chi2=4.03, p=0.045; turning point (peak) AGE~25.0
- d(logit)/dAGE: +0.018 @24, -0.052 @28, -0.121 @32
- P(DISSAVED=1): 0.266 @24 vs 0.194 @32 (diff -0.073)
- Controls: MALE OR=0.82 (p<0.001); log-INCOME OR=1.13 (p<0.001);
  BLACK OR=1.23 (p<0.001); HISPANIC OR=1.10 (p=0.10); BMI ns (p=0.25)
- VIFs all ~1.0 (centering resolved corr(AGE,AGE_2)=0.999 -> -0.05)

### FULL file, unadjusted (n=12,675)
- AGE_c: -0.044 (p<0.001); AGE_c2: -0.009 (p=0.029); P: 0.250 @24 vs 0.186 @32

### DEDUP / non-imputed sensitivity (n=10,486-10,524)
- Unadjusted: AGE_c +0.015 (p=0.118); AGE_c2 -0.004 (p=0.383);
  P: 0.264 @24 vs 0.286 @32 (sign FLIPS slightly positive, ns)
- Adjusted: AGE_c +0.006 (p=0.566); AGE_c2 -0.004 (p=0.413); ns

### Nonparametric check (full file, 3 age bins)
- Predicted P: 24-26: 0.251, 27-29: 0.245 (ns vs 24-26), 30-32: 0.206 (p<0.001)
- Shape: flat 24-29, decline 30-32 (consistent with inverted-U peaking ~25)

### Secondary: SAMESAVE ~ AGE_c + AGE_c2 + controls (full file)
- AGE_c: -0.071 (p<0.001); AGE_c2: -0.010 (p=0.011); SAMESAVE also declines with age.
